  <p>Sustainability has become a serious buying factor for Australian activewear customers. But for a brand owner, sustainability must be practical: verified fabrics, stable quality, realistic MOQ, and transparent claims that can be used in marketing without overpromising.</p>

  <h2>What Sustainable Activewear Means in Production</h2>
  <p>Sustainable activewear is not only about using recycled yarn. It also includes fabric durability, colorfastness, lower defect rates, responsible packaging, and production planning that avoids overstock.</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Recycled polyester or recycled nylon options.</li>
    <li>OEKO-TEX compliant fabric selections when available.</li>
    <li>Durable construction to reduce product returns.</li>
    <li>Smarter MOQ planning to avoid unsold inventory.</li>
    <li>Lower-plastic packaging choices for private label orders.</li>
  </ul>

